    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "13. Terrain",
    "ruleNumber": "13.04",
    "summary": "Low walls and barricades are examples of **Light Terrain**. Light features can shelter models from attacks without slowing their movement. See [Terrain and Movement](vsdata:core-rule/terrain-and-movement) for how models cross them and [Benefit of Cover](vsdata:core-rule/benefit-of-cover) for when a target qualifies. An area with a light feature is [Obscuring](vsdata:core-rule/obscuring).",
